<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Jan Kočí is a systems architect working across Linux, telephony, infrastructure, operations and AI-assisted automation."
>
  <header class="page-intro section-pad">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1>I make complicated systems <span>legible and governable.</span></h1>
    <p>
      I am a Prague-based systems architect with more than eighteen years across Linux,
      telephony, enterprise support, product development and technical leadership.
    </p>
  </header>
  <section class="about-grid section-pad">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I start with operational reality: what exists, who depends on it, what can fail and
        which claims are actually supported by evidence. Architecture follows from that map.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work combines hands-on troubleshooting with system design. I am comfortable moving
        from a broken call flow or Linux service to the governance model that prevents the same
        class of failure from returning.
      </p>
      <h2>What I value</h2>
      <p>
        Clear ownership, reversible change, useful documentation, honest status reporting and
        automation that remains subordinate to human intent.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="principle-panel">
      <p class="section-label">Operating principles</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Reality before assumptions.</li>
        <li>Evidence before confidence theatre.</li>
        <li>Simple systems before fashionable complexity.</li>
        <li>Human approval before meaningful mutation.</li>
        <li>Verification before celebration.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="button primary" href="/cv/">Open the full CV</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
